    "Authentication sessions are synthetic and auth limits are raised in isolated children. This does not validate abuse resistance.",
    "The application clock is fixed to avoid expiry/week rollover during the exercise. Latencies use monotonic wall time; future weekly payout jobs stay scheduled.",
    "The final run uses the current 60-second marketplace/operations cadence with 25 jobs per process; --smoke accelerates it to 500ms. Only these local-safe workers are run, not every main.js maintenance/provider worker.",
    "Simulated bridges use the example configuration idle poll (3s) and heartbeat (30s); no hardware execution or physical print time measured.",
    "Two API processes share a single local WAL database; no multi-host, failover, backup restoration or sustained production capacity proven."
